---
title: Grades
description: Twelve colour grades as CSS — the LUTs — previewed on one picture, plus grain, a vignette and a letterbox. A grade is a filter and, for the film ones, a wash blended over it.
eyebrow: Content creation · Elements
source: src/studio/grade.css
---
<p>An editor’s LUT is a table that maps every colour to another; a CSS grade is the same idea written as a formula — a <code>filter</code> on the picture and, where a range of colours has to move (teal in the shadows, amber in the skin), a tinted layer blended over it. The point of having them here is that a grade can be <strong>previewed on the page</strong> and applied the same way in a browser-rendered video, so the look of the channel is one list of twelve names and not a folder of <code>.cube</code> files. On the whole frame (<code>im-studio-grade-film</code> on <code>im-studio</code>) the picture layers take it and the words do not.</p>
