<h2>Overlays</h2>
{{#example flush=true}}
<div class="frame-grid" style="padding: 1rem">
	<figure><div class="frame-preview"><div class="im-studio" style="--im-studio-w: 960; --im-studio-h: 540"><img class="im-studio-photo" src="{{demo.shots.[0]}}" alt=""><span class="im-studio-grain" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></div><figcaption>im-studio-grain</figcaption></figure>
	<figure><div class="frame-preview"><div class="im-studio" style="--im-studio-w: 960; --im-studio-h: 540"><img class="im-studio-photo" src="{{demo.shots.[0]}}" alt=""><span class="im-studio-vignette" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></div><figcaption>im-studio-vignette</figcaption></figure>
	<figure><div class="frame-preview"><div class="im-studio im-studio-wash" style="--im-studio-w: 960; --im-studio-h: 540"><img class="im-studio-photo" src="{{demo.shots.[0]}}" alt=""></div></div><figcaption>im-studio-wash (the accent, soft light)</figcaption></figure>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p><code>--im-studio-grain</code> (0.35) and <code>--im-studio-vignette</code> (55%) are the strengths; <code>--im-studio-wash</code> and <code>--im-studio-wash-blend</code> make any tint. The grades also sit on a single <code>im-studio-media</code> figure, where the wash takes the figure’s radius.</p>
